⭐ Important Concept (Interview Level)

Serenity does NOT limit you.

Anything Actor needs → create Ability.

Actor can have multiple abilities:

actor.can(BrowseTheWeb.with(driver));
actor.can(CallAnApi.at(baseUrl));
actor.can(UseDatabase.with(connection));
actor.can(UseToken.with(token));
actor.can(UseSSH.with(sshClient));



1. Built-in Abilities Provided by Serenity (Official)

These come from Serenity Screenplay libraries.

✅ Web UI Ability
BrowseTheWeb

Used for Selenium / Playwright style UI automation.

actor.can(BrowseTheWeb.with(driver));


Provides:

WebDriver access

Page interaction

Element lookup

Wait handling

✅ REST API Ability
CallAnApi
actor.can(CallAnApi.at("https://api.test.com"));


Provides:

REST client

Base URL handling

Request execution

✅ Mobile Abilities (Appium)

If using mobile automation:

UseAnAndroidDevice
UseIOSDevice
✅ Serenity Core Ability Interface

All abilities implement:

net.serenitybdd.screenplay.Ability


This is the base contract.

3. Special Serenity Helper Access Pattern

Inside Tasks you often see:

BrowseTheWeb.as(actor).getDriver();


or

CallAnApi.as(actor).getRestClient();


This retrieves the ability from the actor.


4. Hidden Abilities (Indirect)

